sol-1390-finish.log:926:{"body":"## Observed\n`pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-review-tools ui:review -- review workspace-agent-sidebar --critic=fixture` fails identically on clean main (31361f157) and on a feature worktree: `ensureAgentNavigation` times out after 60s — `[data-boring-workspace-part=\"app-left-agent-tree\"]` never reaches count 2 and the \"Open app navigation\" button never appears (spec.ts:37). No page snapshot in error-context.md.\n\n## Expected\nThe registered spec's own fixture server should render the two-agent tree and the review should complete (this is the reviewer-agents entry point named in docs/procedures/visual-review.md).\n\n## Environment\n- OVH VM, 2026-08-23, run from repo root of the primary checkout (main) and from .worktrees/weekend-console-variant — same failure.\n- Two unrelated vite dev servers were live on :5200/:5201 during the runs — port contention with the harness's self-booted server is one suspect; stale/absent built dist consumed by the harness fixture is another (cf. known stale-dist-in-worktree failure mode).\n- Not caused by current PRs: reproduces on untouched main.\n\n## Impact\nThe repo's canonical external UI-review path is unusable, so frontend changes can't get the registered hard-gate review locally.\n\n## Next info needed\nRe-run with no other dev servers up; capture the harness server's stdout and the page HTML at timeout to see what actually rendered.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01UGA4RhWZGNR5QA9Y7dFzCF","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOSLWWUs8AAAABQ4aIXg","author":{"login":"hachej"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Triage 2026-08-26: PR #1406 lands a rewrite of the ui-review replay-selection policy (settled-desktop / strongly-painted-mobile) — likely the same nondeterminism class as this ensureAgentNavigation failure. Retest after #1406 merges; close if green.","createdAt":"2026-08-26T16:11:02Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/hachej/boring-ui/issues/1390#issuecomment-5427857502","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOSLWWUs8AAAABQ_j3-A","author":{"login":"hachej"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Retest 2026-08-27 on origin/main (50edc75a9), clean worktree, 3 back-to-back runs of the issue's exact command: 0/3 passed.\n\n- Run 1: the original symptom — ensureAgentNavigation timeout at spec.ts:37 (tree count never reaches 2, 'Open app navigation' never appears).\n- Runs 2–3: got PAST navigation, then failed UI_REVIEW_HARD_GATES_FAILED on the same 11 mobile/tablet capture states (agent-list, expanded-sessions, pinned-chat, session-row-hover, agent-card-menu, agent-details).\n\nSo the #1406 replay-selection fix did not resolve this spec: the original nav timeout still reproduces intermittently, and a mobile/tablet hard-gate nondeterminism now dominates. Failure mode has broadened — treat both signatures as in-scope for this issue. Repro worktree left at .worktrees/retest-1390.","createdAt":"2026-08-27T06:43:58Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/hachej/boring-ui/issues/1390#issuecomment-5435357176","viewerDidAuthor":true},{"id":"IC_kwDOSLWWUs8AAAABQ_quIg","author":{"login":"hachej"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"Third independent sighting of the mobile/tablet hard-gate nondeterminism: the UI Review gate fails on PRs #1423 and #1424 (unrelated ui-kit one-liners) with different violation IDs per run, this time on workspace-command-palette mobile states. Combined with the 2026-08-27 retest (2/3 runs failing hard-gates on workspace-agent-sidebar mobile/tablet states), the mobile hard-gate flake is now the dominant signature of this issue and is blocking unrelated PRs. Raising priority accordingly.","createdAt":"2026-08-27T06:57:21Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/hachej/boring-ui/issues/1390#issuecomment-5435469346","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDOSLWWUs8AAAACgmAEgA","name":"bug","description":"Boring v2 category: something is broken","color":"D73A4A"},{"id":"LA_kwDOSLWWUs8AAAACrBOD8A","name":"ready-for-agent","description":"Boring v2: agent can plan or implement safely","color":"0E8A16"}],"number":1390,"state":"OPEN","title":"ui-review: workspace-agent-sidebar spec fails at ensureAgentNavigation on clean main","url":"https://github.com/hachej/boring-ui/issues/1390"}
sol-thermo-1431.log:14:Code-thermo review gate for PR #1431 on hachej/boring-ui (ui-review harness determinism: capture settling, one-shot agent-discovery reload, pointer-model correction — fixes #1390). gh pr diff 1431, gh pr view 1431, gh issue view 1390 --comments for history. Adversarial focus: (1) is the 5/5 consecutive proof claim in the body real and reproducible in principle (check the run evidence described); (2) does the pointer-model change weaken the coarse-pointer hard gate anywhere (390px fine-pointer no longer touch — could a real touch device config now escape the 44px gate?); (3) does the discovery reload mask real app failures (one retry could hide a legit regression — is it bounded and logged?); (4) weakened assertions in the 94+ harness tests. Worktree with code: /home/ubuntu/projects/boring-ui-v2/.worktrees/retest-1390 (branch fix/1390-ui-review-determinism). Post ONE comment via gh pr comment 1431: SHIP/REVISE, ranked findings, verified-vs-trusted. If SHIP: gh pr edit 1431 --add-label ready-for-human. No merge/push. End with the verdict.
sol-thermo-1431.log:454:{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwODEyNDYz","is_bot":false,"login":"hachej","name":"Julien Hurault"},"baseRefName":"main","baseRefOid":"f990c42f4905b1d34a17773706a2034f2464f518","body":"## Root causes and mechanisms\n\n- **Mobile/tablet hard-gate nondeterminism:** screenshot capture and DOM hard-gate collection could observe different animation/layout frames. The harness now freezes CSS motion, waits for fonts plus two animation frames, and keeps that freeze active across both screenshot and hard-gate collection before cleaning it up.\n- **Terminal empty agent roster:** the app client performs one-shot agent discovery; a rejected initial discovery cannot recover by waiting longer. Sidebar readiness now spends an initial bounded wait, reloads once, then retries readiness so discovery/hydration gets one clean restart.\n- **Pointer-model mismatch:** compact width and coarse-pointer capability are separate signals. Registered Playwright mobile capture opts into touch explicitly. Bombadil cannot emulate pointer capability, and its CI browser may report a coarse pointer even at desktop width, so the touch-target property was removed from Bombadil rather than inferred from the host browser. The command-palette hard-gate contract/spec revision is bumped accordingly.\n- **Bombadil replay divergence:** opening app navigation reveals the compact `Search⌘K` trigger asynchronously. The action policy now emits one settle `Wait` after the navigation-open click before allowing the revealed trigger, keeping generated and replayed action sets aligned.\n\n## App-fix dependency\n\nThe deterministic harness correctly exposed the genuine 20px `Archived` control on coarse-pointer sidebar states. That app defect was fixed and merged to `main` by #1430 (closing #1429); this branch is based on that merge. No app code is changed here.\n\n## Proof\n\n- `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-review-tools test` — 95/95 passed.\n- `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-review-tools typecheck` — passed with no errors.\n- Exact consecutive review command: `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-review-tools ui:review -- review workspace-agent-sidebar --critic=fixture`\n  - Run 1: PASS — 1 passed (1.1m)\n  - Run 2: PASS — 1 passed (1.1m)\n  - Run 3: PASS — 1 passed (1.2m)\n  - Run 4: PASS — 1 passed (1.7m)\n  - Run 5: PASS — 1 passed (1.1m)\n  - Result: **5/5 consecutive green**\n- Thermonuclear maintainability review: clean; no material findings.\n- GitHub CI run `33101687058`: all required checks passed, including UI Review.\n\nFixes #1390\n","comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOSLWWUs8AAAABRHRQSg","author":{"login":"hachej"},"authorAssociation":"OWNER","body":"## Proof of work\n\nFinal head: `65f32725057e5583a064c8807b352087eda15bd8`\n\n- Capture stability freezes motion and keeps screenshot + DOM gates on one settled frame.\n- Sidebar readiness performs one bounded discovery reload before its final retry.\n- Playwright explicitly models touch with `hasTouch`; Bombadil no longer infers pointer capability.\n- Bombadil inserts one settle action after opening app navigation so generated and replayed action sets agree.\n\nValidation:\n\n- `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-review-tools test` — 95/95 PASS.\n- `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-review-tools typecheck` — PASS.\n- `pnpm --filter @hachej/boring-ui-review-tools ui:review -- review workspace-agent-sidebar --critic=fixture` — 5/5 consecutive PASS on the final runtime tree (1.1m, 1.1m, 1.2m, 1.7m, 1.1m).\n- GitHub CI run `33101687058` — PASS, including UI Review.\n- Independent thermonuclear review — clean after follow-up findings were closed and re-reviewed.\n\nThe PR remains open and unmerged for owner validation.\n","createdAt":"2026-08-27T18:22:50Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/hachej/boring-ui/pull/1431#issuecomment-5443440714","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-08-27T13:45:26Z","authors":[{"email":"julien.hurault@sumeo.io","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwODEyNDYz","login":"hachej","name":"hachej"},{"email":"noreply@anthropic.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","login":"claude","name":"Claude Fable 5"}],"committedDate":"2026-08-27T13:45:26Z","messageBody":"…er model\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MQgxe5KTr2N2pjgjgKPXHK","messageHeadline":"#1390 fix(ui-review): deterministic capture + discovery retry + point…","oid":"f70078b04f26b11d520deeaed6c09b1a87e432bd"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-27T15:21:43Z","authors":[{"email":"julien.hurault@sumeo.io","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwODEyNDYz","login":"hachej","name":"hachej"}],"committedDate":"2026-08-27T15:21:43Z","messageBody":"Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MQgxe5KTr2N2pjgjgKPXHK","messageHeadline":"#1390 fix(ui-review): keep Bombadil pointer model capability-free","oid":"0812dc40cb3c5e440fa8552d82eb279327c8254a"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-27T16:46:29Z","authors":[{"email":"julien.hurault@sumeo.io","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwODEyNDYz","login":"hachej","name":"hachej"}],"committedDate":"2026-08-27T16:46:29Z","messageBody":"Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MQgxe5KTr2N2pjgjgKPXHK","messageHeadline":"#1390 fix(ui-review): assign touch policy to Playwright","oid":"7b08b696c7854b80d97f1ca74dfe3150ddfc8480"},{"authoredDate":"2026-08-27T18:03:47Z","authors":[{"email":"julien.hurault@sumeo.io","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwODEyNDYz","login":"hachej","name":"hachej"}],"committedDate":"2026-08-27T18:03:47Z","messageBody":"Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MQgxe5KTr2N2pjgjgKPXHK","messageHeadline":"#1390 fix(ui-review): settle navigation before Bombadil replay","oid":"65f32725057e5583a064c8807b352087eda15bd8"}],"files":[{"path":"tools/ui-review/e2e/review.spec.ts","additions":22,"deletions":19,"ch